[b][size=150]appleTV Plugin 1.8.8[/size][/b]
[i]Apple TV 4K (4th gen) & tvOS 27 support, a more reliable connection layer, and easy Apple TV replacement[/i]

[b]────────────────────────────────────────[/b]

[b][size=125]Why a custom pyatv build?[/size][/b]

The plugin is built on [url=https://pyatv.dev]pyatv[/url]. Upstream pyatv hasn't had a commit or release since [b]19 June 2026 (v0.18.0)[/b]. Since then, the community has submitted dozens of fixes that are still waiting to be merged, including support for new hardware and tvOS 27.

From 1.8.7 the plugin installs pyatv from [url=https://github.com/Ghawken/pyatv/tree/indigo]Ghawken/pyatv (indigo branch)[/url]. That branch is upstream 0.18.0 plus a selected set of those pending fixes, all passing pyatv's full test suite (1325 passed). Current version: [b]0.18.0.post2[/b]. If upstream starts releasing again, the plugin will move back to the official package.

Indigo installs the new library automatically when you update the plugin.

[b]────────────────────────────────────────[/b]

[b][size=125]Library improvements (pyatv)[/size][/b]

[b]New hardware & tvOS 27[/b]
[list]
[*][b]Apple TV 4K (4th generation) recognised[/b]: the new AppleTV18,1 shows as "Apple TV 4K (gen 4)" running tvOS, not "Unknown". [url=https://github.com/postlund/pyatv/pull/2949]#2949[/url]
[*][b]AirPlay PIN pairing fixed on tvOS 27[/b]: tvOS 27 could stop the pairing PIN from appearing on screen. pyatv now sends the client name tvOS 27 expects. [url=https://github.com/postlund/pyatv/pull/2894]#2894[/url]
[*][b]Pairing errors reported instead of hanging[/b]: a rejected pairing now fails immediately, instead of hanging ~10 seconds and then failing with a confusing error. [url=https://github.com/postlund/pyatv/pull/2920]#2920[/url]
[*][b]Clearer authentication errors[/b] for AirPlay remote control. [url=https://github.com/postlund/pyatv/pull/2924]#2924[/url]
[/list]

[b]Connection reliability[/b]
[list]
[*][b]No leaked connections on failed connects[/b]: a failed connection attempt used to leave network connections open. With the plugin's automatic retries, a sleeping or offline device could pile these up. [url=https://github.com/postlund/pyatv/pull/2945]#2945[/url]
[*][b]Companion protocol error replies[/b] are now treated as errors, not as successful responses. [url=https://github.com/postlund/pyatv/pull/2939]#2939[/url]
[/list]

[b]Discovery (finding your devices)[/b]
[list]
[*][b]By-IP scans wait for all services[/b]: these scans used to stop early and could miss services that are slow to appear, e.g. Companion just after the Apple TV wakes (this affects power state and app launching). [url=https://github.com/postlund/pyatv/pull/2911]#2911[/url]
[*][b]Fallback scan asks for every service type[/b]. [url=https://github.com/postlund/pyatv/pull/2930]#2930[/url]
[*][b]Unusual device names no longer abort a scan[/b]. [url=https://github.com/postlund/pyatv/pull/2936]#2936[/url]
[*][b]Malformed network packets ignored[/b]. [url=https://github.com/postlund/pyatv/pull/2926]#2926[/url]
[*][b]Multi-VLAN / mDNS-reflector networks[/b] (UniFi, Firewalla, Avahi): devices are no longer mixed up (wrong models shown, or every device appearing to be in deep sleep). [url=https://github.com/postlund/pyatv/pull/2931]#2931[/url]
[/list]

[b]Playback & device state[/b]
[list]
[*][b]Playback position NaN fixed[/b]: fixes broken position and remaining-time calculations for some apps. [url=https://github.com/postlund/pyatv/pull/2897]#2897[/url]
[*][b]No bogus volume updates[/b] when the device doesn't report a volume. [url=https://github.com/postlund/pyatv/pull/2935]#2935[/url]
[*][b]HomePod stereo pairs show as On[/b] while playing. [url=https://github.com/postlund/pyatv/pull/2917]#2917[/url]
[*][b]Audio streaming deadlock fixed[/b]: streaming some URLs to AirPlay devices could stall with "failed to init decoder". [url=https://github.com/postlund/pyatv/pull/2850]#2850[/url]
[*][b]AirPlay feature detection fixed[/b] for some third-party receivers (e.g. LG TVs). [url=https://github.com/postlund/pyatv/pull/2942]#2942[/url]
[/list]

[b]────────────────────────────────────────[/b]

[b][size=125]Plugin improvements[/size][/b]

[b]1.8.8[/b]
[list]
[*]Uses pyatv 0.18.0.post2, which adds Apple TV 4K (4th gen) support.
[/list]

[b]1.8.7[/b]
[list]
[*][b]Fixed connections constantly dropping and reconnecting after re-pairing[/b]: an orphaned background connection could fight the new one. Old connections now always shut down properly, and a device can only ever have one connection.
[*]Switched to the custom pyatv build above.
[/list]

[b]1.8.6[/b]
[list]
[*][b]New "Reset Device" button[/b] in the device config dialog, for replacing an Apple TV (e.g. a new unit on the same IP). It stops the current connection and clears the saved pairing credentials, identifier and MAC address (it keeps the IP address).
[*][b]Start Connection[/b] now pairs with whatever Apple TV is at the device's IP after a reset.
[*]A log message now explains when no matching Apple TV is found. Previously it failed silently.
[/list]

[b]────────────────────────────────────────[/b]

[b][size=125]Replacing an Apple TV[/size][/b]

[list=1]
[*]Open the Indigo device → [b]Edit Device Settings[/b]
[*]Press [b]Reset Device[/b]
[*]Press [b]Start Connection[/b], enter the PIN shown on the TV, and press [b]Submit PinCode[/b]
[*]Press [b]Save[/b]
[/list]
